---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const d='/equipment/03-11/',nist='https://www.nist.gov/system/files/documents/2017/05/09/Manual_RTA.pdf#page=1',mpt='https://kb.encs.vancouver.wsu.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/7/2023/08/rtp600xp_manual-1.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="RTP-600xp de-energized display" description="Inspect a metric RTP cabinet and check purely geometric clearance of an inert dry display fixture." wide={true}><article id="rtp600" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/03-11/">← Equipment 03-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#rtp-evidence">Reference sheet</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">03-11 / DE-ENERGIZED DISPLAY</p><h2>How much room does the dummy have?</h2><p class="eq-lede">Extend the model’s dry display drawer and compare a 150 mm placeholder against two schematic rails. This first pass shows a cabinet and a fit check, not a process.</p></header>
<div class="r-cols"><section><h3>Modular Process Technology RTP-600xp</h3><canvas id="rtp-model" aria-label="Orbitable de-energized RTP-600xp cabinet, display drawer and terminal"></canvas><p id="rtp-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="rtp-front">Whole station / reset view</button><button id="rtp-tray">Display drawer close-up</button><button id="rtp-rear">Rear</button><p>The silver handle toggles the schematic drawer. Front panel details are inert decorative geometry.</p></section>
<section><h3>Dry geometry only</h3><label>Dummy disc diameter<select id="rtp-size"><option value="150">150 mm</option><option value="100">100 mm</option><option value="200">200 mm</option><option value="220">220 mm</option></select></label><label>Transverse center shift, mm<input id="rtp-offset" type="number" min="-20" max="20" step="any" value="0"/></label><button id="rtp-drawer">Extend display drawer</button><button id="rtp-check">Check clearance</button><button id="rtp-reset">Restore display</button><p id="rtp-status" role="status"></p><p id="rtp-read"></p><button id="rtp-export">Download inspection JSON</button><p><a href={d+'example.json'}>Example inspection</a>. The two signed margins are measured from the left and right schematic rails. This does not check insertion, vertical clearance, process eligibility or any real wafer.</p></section></div>
<section id="rtp-evidence"><h3>Configuration and evidence</h3><p>MPT RTP-600xp reference exterior. <a href={nist}>NIST's front installation photograph, cover</a> shows the benchtop cabinet, controller and offset monitor. The <a href={mpt}>manufacturer's installation specification MAN-600xp-OPER-3.0, §6.4.1, printed p. 112</a> gives rounded 610 mm width, 350 mm height and 580 mm depth for the oven cabinet. The modeled static cabinet takes these metric nominal values. Console, bench, hose silhouette, internal blanking surfaces, display tray travel, and abstract rails are original illustrative estimates.</p><div class="r-cols"><figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original RTP-600xp de-energized station overview"/><figcaption>Original cabinet/monitor overview, inspired by the NIST reference.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={d+'tray.webp'} alt="Original dry display tray with teal placeholder"/><figcaption>Original authored dry layout; not actual machine internals.</figcaption></figure></div><p>The dry check uses 103 mm on each side of the authored centerline. For dummy radius r and lateral offset x, left clearance is 103+x−r and right is 103−x−r, in mm. Only sign and lateral clearance are inferred. No internal optical or heating components, process controls, recipes, or real operations are represented.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Independent geometry case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>150 mm centered</td><td>28 mm each side</td><td>28 / 28, fits</td></tr><tr><td>200 mm, shift +3</td><td>0 mm right</td><td>0 mm; tangent</td></tr><tr><td>200 mm, shift +5</td><td>−2 mm right</td><td>−2 mm; outside</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'rtp600xp.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'dry-carrier.mjs'}>Geometry and states</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR bounds, nominal drawer</a>. Not verified on a headset.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/03-11/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#rtp600 .r-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.12fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#rtp600 section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#rtp600 :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#rtp600 label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.35rem 0}#rtp600 label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#rtp600 button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#rtp600 button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#rtp600 button:disabled{opacity:.5}#rtp-model{display:block;width:100%;height:330px;touch-action:none}#rtp600 figure{margin:.5rem 0}#rtp600 figure img{width:100%}#rtp600 table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#rtp600 td,#rtp600 th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}@media(max-width:780px){#rtp600 .r-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#rtp-model{height:280px}}</style>
